# Backend (.NET)

## Entry & config

- `Program.cs` — DI, migrate DB, seed roles/admin, map controllers, Hangfire dashboard
- `appsettings.json` + env: `ConnectionStrings__DefaultConnection`, `Jwt__*`, `Ai__OpenRouterKey`, `Ai__Model_1..3`
- Extensions: `Extensions/DatabaseExtensions.cs`, `IdentityExtensions`, `HangfireExtensions`, `ApplicationServicesExtensions.cs`

## Layers

| Layer | Location |
|-------|----------|
| Controllers | `Controllers/*Controller.cs` — route prefix `api/[controller]` |
| Services | `Services/`, interfaces in `Services/Abstractions/` |
| Jobs | `Jobs/` — Hangfire; enqueue from `ResourceService` |
| Entities | `Entities/Resources/`, `Entities/Tagging/`, `Entities/Users/` |
| DTOs | `DTOs/` |
| EF | `Data/AppDbContext.cs`, `Migrations/` |

## Controllers → services

- `ResourcesController` → `IResourceService` (create, delete, status, retry)
- `InboxController` / `VaultController` → `IResourceService` (paged lists, mix, get by id)
- `CategoriesController` → `ICategoryService`
- `PreferencesController` → `IUserPreferencesService`
- `AuthController` → `IIdentityService`

## Jobs

- `UrlIngestionJob.ProcessAsync(resourceId)` — sets `Processing`, fetches content, chains AI job
- `AiAnalysisJob` — scoring using user preferences
- `ErrorRecoveryJob` — recurring hourly (`HangfireExtensions.ScheduleRecurringJobs`)

## Adding features

1. Entity/DTO changes → migration: `dotnet ef migrations add Name -p KnowledgeOS.Backend`
2. Business logic in service, thin controller
3. Background work: interface in `Jobs/Abstractions/`, register scoped in `ApplicationServicesExtensions`
4. New fetcher: implement `IContentFetcher`, register in `AddApplicationServices`

Use `ICurrentUserService.UserId` for ownership; use `IgnoreQueryFilters()` only in jobs/admin paths.
